# MCG Convoy luxury UI

Private club instrument cluster. Graphite + champagne. Cormorant for Latin brand marks. IBM Plex Sans Thai for Thai UI. Thai-default + equal-weight EN toggle.

## Product rules

- No rewards, copy, or visuals based on speed, racing, or beating ETA.
- No public late shaming. Late badges stay private.
- Driving mode: passengers operate the map; drivers get locked dense inputs.
- Generic vehicle silhouettes only — no manufacturer marks.

## Visual system

- Steal patterns from Motion / Vaul / NumberFlow / Base UI / Phosphor — never Aceternity/Magic UI/shadcn default look.
- Color with purpose. Build from black. Contrast ≥ 4.5:1.
- Live map is the hero: OpenFreeMap graphite/champagne, 150 m geofence, heading needles.
- One motion per navigation. `prefers-reduced-motion` disables NumberFlow/Vaul spring.
- No custom cursor, particles, Lenis, or sitewide GSAP inside LIFF.

## Screen jobs

- Thai club words are first-class: จุดนัดพบ, รถนำ, รถปิดท้าย, พักปั๊ม.
- PDPA: location consent is purpose-limited and withdrawable (Pause/Stop).
- Dates in `th` use `th-TH` + Asia/Bangkok (พ.ศ.).
- Landing: foyer + ritual (invite → convoy → arrive).
- Invite: privacy + PDPA checkbox before join.
- Live HUD: peek = action (share + ETA); expanded = overview (roster).
- Arrival: confirm ritual, disputes private.
- Summary: safe aggregates + badges only.

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — SaaS feature grid + speed leaderboard
<h2>Fastest arrival</h2>

// ✅ GOOD — punctuality, never speed
<p>Arrive together — never race.</p>
```
